# NEYORA Brand Rules

NEYORA is a premium natural-food brand. Tagline: **GROWN FOR LIFE.**

The first product is fresh oyster mushrooms, but NEYORA is a natural-food
company, not a mushroom company. Never hardcode mushroom-specific assumptions
into schema, routes, components or copy.

Full reference: `docs/BRAND_GUIDELINES.md`. Read it before making visual choices.

## Brand personality

Natural · Premium · Warm · Modern · Trustworthy · Healthy · Earth-connected

Not: rustic, cute, techy, corporate, clinical, hippie.

## Colours (use the CSS tokens, never raw hex in components)

| Token | Hex | CSS var |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Deep Forest Green | `#123C2A` | `--color-forest` |
| Botanical Green | `#3F7D3A` | `--color-botanical` |
| Fresh Leaf | `#8BAF35` | `--color-leaf` |
| Golden Green | `#C6B83A` | `--color-golden` |
| Warm Ivory | `#F6F0E3` | `--color-ivory` |
| Mushroom Beige | `#D8C9B5` | `--color-beige` |
| Earth | `#2B2923` | `--color-earth` |

Use Tailwind utilities generated from these (`bg-forest`, `text-earth`,
`border-beige`, …). Do not invent new colours.

## Never use

- Blue, cyan, aqua, teal, indigo, violet
- Neon / fluorescent green
- Generic SaaS gradients (purple→blue, blue→cyan, aurora meshes)
- Generic AI imagery, flat vector farms, leaf doodles
- Cheap stock-photo aesthetic
- Pure `#000` or `#FFF` as a large field

## Colour proportion — 70/20/8/2

70% ivory/beige · 20% photography · 8% forest green · 2% leaf + golden.
**If a screenshot reads as "green", it is wrong.**

## The gradient

`#123C2A → #3F7D3A → #8BAF35 → #C6B83A`, left to right. Allowed in exactly
three places: the wordmark, a hairline section rule, and rarely one short piece
of display text. Never on buttons, cards, backgrounds, icons or sections.

## Typography

- Display: **Fraunces** (`font-display`), large and tight (`-0.02em`).
- Body/UI: **Inter** (`font-sans`).
- Eyebrow: Inter 12px, uppercase, `0.18em` tracking, botanical green, once per section.
- Body measure ≤ 68ch.

## Design principles

Use: generous whitespace (96–160px section padding), asymmetry, hairline
`1px` beige borders instead of shadows, small radii (2–6px), editorial image
captions, one clear action per section, restrained motion (fade + 8–16px
translate, 200–500ms, honour `prefers-reduced-motion`).

Avoid: rounded-2xl shadowed cards in 3-up grids, glassmorphism, frosted
navbars, icon-in-coloured-circle feature rows, emoji icons, parallax,
scroll-jacking, animated counters, template-like SaaS layouts.

## Accessibility

WCAG 2.2 AA. Leaf (`#8BAF35`) and Golden (`#C6B83A`) **fail AA on ivory for
body text** — use them only for ≥24px display type, borders or focus rings.
Focus ring: 2px leaf, 2px offset, always visible. Real alt text everywhere.

## Engineering rules that protect the brand

- Marketing copy lives in `/content`, never in JSX. If you find yourself typing
  a headline into a component, move it to the content file and read it from
  `lib/content`.
- Server components by default; `'use client'` only where interaction requires
  it.
- Images need explicit width, height and alt text. The content schema enforces
  all three — a missing one fails the build, and that is intentional.
- Never introduce a database, an account system or a paid service without being
  asked. The site is static on purpose; see ARCHITECTURE.md §1.
